issue_context.body:
The client-go Kubernetes fake client can’t list pods after an eviction is created.


**What happened**:

https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/71599 introduced a regression in the fake clientset, where creating an Eviction causes listing pods to fail with `item[0]: can't assign or convert v1beta1.Eviction into v1.Pod`. This is because the Eviction is stored next to the pods, so listing the pods also lists the evictions which then fail to get assigned to the PodList.

**What you expected to happen**:

Listing pods to work after creating an eviction

**How to reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)**:

```

package main

import (
        v1 "k8s.io/api/core/v1"
        policy "k8s.io/api/policy/v1beta1"
        meta_v1 "k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/apis/meta/v1"
        "k8s.io/client-go/kubernetes/fake"
)

func main() {
        client := fake.NewSimpleClientset(
                &v1.Pod{
                        ObjectMeta: meta_v1.ObjectMeta{
                                Name:      "pod-1",
                                Namespace: "default",
                        },
                },
        )
        client.CoreV1().Pods("default").Evict(&policy.Eviction{
                ObjectMeta: meta_v1.ObjectMeta{
                        Name: "pod-1",
                },
        })
        _, err := client.CoreV1().Pods("default").List(meta_v1.ListOptions{})
        // err: item[0]: can't assign or convert v1beta1.Eviction into v1.Pod
}
```

**Anything else we need to know?**:

To fix this we could filter out the resources that have a ‘subresource’ when listing, or not store the evictions at all.

**Environment**:
- client-go version: `k8s.io/client-go v0.0.0-20190620085101-78d2af792bab`
